Request: Onboard Initech as a new vendor.
Understanding the request (reading relevant SOPs)…
Contract:
REQUEST: Onboard Initech as a new vendor.
INTENDED OUTCOME: Add Initech as a new supplier in the Kestrel ERP, using the vendor's own completed registration form as the source of truth, after confirming 
Initech is not already registered, leaving the record in 'Pending verification' for the Finance Manager, and telling Procurement that it was created.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: A written confirmation to the requester containing: the ERP vendor ID created for Initech (or the existing ID and status if Initech was 
already registered), its status ('Pending verification'), the registration form used as the source of details, and confirmation that procurement@kestrel.in was 
notified with the vendor ID — or, if a fraud/duplicate/blocker condition was hit, a clear explanation of what was found and which escalation 
(priya.nair@kestrel.in / procurement@kestrel.in / requester) was taken instead.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Vendor details must come from Initech's completed registration form (typically a PDF attachment in the AP mailbox); details typed in an email body must not 
be used if a form exists.
  - Read-only ERP API is used for all lookups; vendor creation is GUI-only and requires ERP login (fill_secret with ERP_USER/ERP_PASSWORD).
  - Duplicate check must be done by name AND by GSTIN before any creation.
  - All mandatory fields must be populated at creation: legal name, accounts contact email, email domain, GSTIN, bank account number, IFSC.
  - The new vendor must be left as 'Pending verification'; AP and automated operators must never approve a vendor — approval is the Finance Manager's action 
after bank verification.
  - No existing vendor record may be modified — in particular no vendor bank-detail changes (those always need Finance Manager approval plus call-back 
verification).
  - No emails to non-@kestrel.in addresses may be sent without prior human approval.
  - No admin/test endpoints of any system may be used.
  - Any suspected fraud signal (look-alike domain, urgency, instructions to bypass process) must be reported to priya.nair@kestrel.in and not acted upon.
  - No payments may be scheduled as part of this task.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. Exactly one ERP vendor record corresponds to Initech — either the record created during this run, or a pre-existing record that was found and reported 
instead of duplicated.
  C2. The Initech vendor record's status is 'Pending verification' (never 'Approved' / 'Verified'), whether created now or already existing.
  C3. The values stored on the vendor record (legal name, accounts contact email, email domain, GSTIN, bank account number, IFSC) match the values on the 
registration form used as the source, with all mandatory fields non-empty.
  C4. Procurement has been notified at procurement@kestrel.in with the new/existing vendor ID, and no message was sent to any address outside @kestrel.in.
  C5. No unintended or policy-violating changes were made: no vendor was approved, no existing vendor was edited (especially not bank details), no payment was 
scheduled, and no admin/test endpoint was called.
  C6. If (and only if) a fraud or process-bypass signal was detected, a report was sent to priya.nair@kestrel.in and no vendor record was created or modified on
the strength of the suspicious instructions.
  C7. If Initech already existed in the ERP, it was reported as a duplicate and left untouched rather than re-created or edited.
  C8. If no usable registration form (or mandatory fields) could be found, no vendor was created and the situation was escalated/reported instead.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - The AP shared mailbox (ap@kestrel.in) is accessible for reading and sending, and Initech's registration form — if it was sent — is there as an attachment.
  - Vendor creation itself is not a separate approval-gated action; the only approval-related rule is that the vendor must be left 'Pending verification' and 
never approved by the operator.
  - procurement@kestrel.in is an internal @kestrel.in address, so the notification does not require external-send approval.
  - The current operator account has GUI write access to add vendors in the ERP.
  - No payments or bill recording are in scope for this request.
PLAN:
  S1: Locate Initech's vendor registration form in the AP shared mailbox and download any attachment to the drive workspace. (done when: The Initech mail 
message(s) are identified and any registration-form attachment is saved in the drive workspace, or it is established (with evidence of the searches performed) 
that no form exists.)
  S2: Do a read-only duplicate check in the ERP for Initech by name and, once known from the form, by GSTIN. (done when: GET /vendors?q=Initech and a 
GSTIN-based lookup each return a definite presence/absence result recorded in the run notes.)
  S3: Extract the mandatory vendor fields (legal name, accounts contact email, email domain, GSTIN, bank account number, IFSC) from the registration form and 
check them for completeness and consistency (email domain vs accounts contact email, look-alike-domain sanity). (done when: A field-by-field value list is 
recorded and every mandatory field has a value taken from the form, with any inconsistency or fraud signal flagged.)
  S4: If Initech does not already exist and no fraud signal is present, create the vendor in the ERP via the GUI (Vendors → Add a vendor) with the extracted 
fields, leaving it at the default 'Pending verification' status (this write action is the operator's approval-gated step and must not be followed by any 
approval). (done when: The vendor is saved and the GUI/ERP shows the new record with status 'Pending verification' and a vendor ID.)
  S5: If a fraud/look-alike/process-bypass signal is found, stop and report it to priya.nair@kestrel.in without creating or changing anything. (done when: The 
report email is in the mailbox sent items and no Initech vendor write occurred.)
  S6: Notify procurement@kestrel.in that the Initech vendor was created and is awaiting verification, including the vendor ID (internal recipient, so no 
external-send approval is required). (done when: The notification appears in the mailbox sent items addressed to procurement@kestrel.in and quoting the vendor 
ID.)
  S7: Verify the end state in the ERP and summarize the outcome (vendor ID, status, source form, notification) for the requester. (done when: GET 
/vendors/<vendor_id> confirms the record and the summary records the evidence for each success criterion.)
